-- title:
--   Tower K⊆ fieldOver ⊆ modularFunctionFieldBar, integral at prime level
-- statement:
--   Fix a natural number $N \neq 0$ and an intermediate field $K$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$. Inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}((q))$ the project's subfield `fieldOver N K` is generated by the constant series of elements of $K$ together with the two Laurent series `jqModC` ($= j(q)$, the $q$-expansion of $j$ with coefficients read in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$) and `jqNModC` ($= j(q^N)$, its image under the $N$-fold substitution `qExpand`); `modularFunctionFieldBar N` is the intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}((q))/\overline{\mathbb Q}$ generated by the coefficientwise image of $\mathbb Q\bigl(j(q^d) : d \mid N\bigr)$. This module equips these two fields with the algebra structures making them a tower. The constant-series map $c \mapsto \mathrm{C}(c)$ realises $K$ as a subfield of `fieldOver N K`, compatibly with the structural map $\overline{\mathbb Q} \to \overline{\mathbb Q}((q))$; the containment `fieldOver N K` $\subseteq$ `modularFunctionFieldBar N` (proved from the facts that the coefficient embedding carries $j$ to `jqModC` and commutes with `qExpand`) supplies the second algebra map; and the resulting scalar towers $K \to$ `fieldOver N K` $\to$ `modularFunctionFieldBar N` and `fieldOver N K` $\to$ `modularFunctionFieldBar N` $\to \overline{\mathbb Q}((q))$ are recorded, as are the characteristic-zero instances for $\overline{\mathbb Q}((q))$ and for `fieldOver N K`.
--
--   The last section specialises to a prime $q$, the level being written throughout as $1 \cdot q$. Since the divisors of $q$ are $1$ and $q$, the coefficient embedding sends $\mathbb Q\bigl(j(q^d) : d \mid q\bigr)$ into `fieldOver (1 * q) K`; combined with the fact that every constant $c \in \overline{\mathbb Q}$ is integral over `fieldOver (1 * q) K` (being algebraic over $\mathbb Q$), this yields that `modularFunctionFieldBar (1 * q)` is an integral — hence algebraic — extension of `fieldOver (1 * q) K`.
--
--   **Relation to Mathlib.** The Laurent/Hahn series, intermediate fields, `IsScalarTower` and integrality API are Mathlib's; `fieldOver`, `modularFunctionFieldBar`, `jqModC`, `jqNModC` and `qExpand` are the project's own notions, and the algebra maps here are built from Mathlib's subfield and subring inclusions.
--
--   **Where it is used.** These instances make a place of `fieldOver N K` over $K$, and the restriction along `fieldOver N K` $\subseteq$ `modularFunctionFieldBar N` of a place of the geometric modular function field, well-typed; the prime-level integrality is what restriction of places along this inclusion requires. They serve the local analysis of $X_0(q)$ at the nodes of its reduction, used in the level-lowering half of the argument.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Definitions/Def_ModularCurve_NodeDescentTower.lean

